   401	>    and `(mu_0,corr_0)=(1,0)`; `A_F = D_1 ∪ D_0` with `D_1 != D_0`.
   402	> 2. `s_1 = 1`, `a_{D_1} = 2`; `s_0 ∈ {1,2,3}`, `a_{D_0} = 4 - s_0`.
   403	> 3. `Br = D_1`. `q` is finite étale of degree `4` over `C^2 - D_1` with
   404	>    connected total space, so `pi_1(C^2 - D_1)` surjects onto a transitive
   405	>    subgroup of `S_4` generated by conjugates of one transposition, i.e. onto
   406	>    `S_4`. In particular `pi_1(C^2 - D_1)` is **non-abelian**.
   407	> 4. Every affine branch of `D_1` and of `D_0` is smooth. Every `p ∈ Sing D_1`
   408	>    with `p ∉ D_0` has exactly two branches, `a_p = 0`, and local monodromy
   409	>    generated by two **disjoint** transpositions (cycle type `(2,2)`).
   410	> 5. Writing `D~_1 = P^1 - {r_1 pts}` (`= l_1'`, since `s_1=1`),
   411	>    `D~_0 = P^1 - {c_0 pts}`, `k_p` the number of branches of `D_0` at `p`,
   412	>    `t_p` the number of points of `l_0'` over `p`, and `eps_p >= 0` the number
   413	>    of contracted (`L_C`) fibre points over `p`, the aggregate Euler identity is
   414	>    ```
   415	>      2 r_1 + s_0 c_0 + sum_{p ∈ Sing A_F} (s_0 k_p - t_p) + sum_p eps_p
   416	>          = 1 + 2 s_0 ,
   417	>    ```
   418	>    all displayed summands being `>= 0`. Hence **`c_0 = 1`, i.e.
   419	>    `D~_0 ≅ A^1`**, and `r_1 = 1` (so `D~_1 ≅ A^1`) except possibly when
   420	>    `s_0 = 3`, where `r_1 = 2` (`D~_1 ≅ C^*`) is also numerically admissible.
   421	>
   422	> *Proof.* (1) is the budget plus §4.2. (2): over generic `p ∈ D_1`,
   423	> `a_{D_1} + 2 s_1 = 4` with `a_{D_1} >= 1` forces `s_1 = 1`, `a_{D_1} = 2`;
   424	> over generic `p ∈ D_0`, `a_{D_0} + s_0 = 4`. (3): Lemma 3.1 with `Br = D_1`;
   425	> transitivity and generation from Lemma 3.2; `S_4` is the only transitive
   426	> subgroup of `S_4` generated by transpositions. (4): Lemma 3.3 for smoothness;
   427	> at `p ∈ Sing D_1 - D_0` the fibre relation `2 beta_p + a_p + eps_p = 4` with
   428	> `beta_p >= 2` (two smooth branches, `l_1' ≅ D~_1`) forces `beta_p = 2`,
   429	> `a_p = eps_p = 0`; the local monodromy orbits then have sizes `(2,2)`, and two
   430	> transpositions generating a group with orbit sizes `2,2` are disjoint.
   431	> (5): substitute `chi_i = chi_c(D~_i) - n_i` into the aggregate identity
   432	> `sum_i (4-a_i) chi_i = 3 - 4 s + sum_p a_p` (proved as in Lemma 3.4, with
   433	> `D_i^0 = D_i - Sing A_F`), and eliminate `sum_p a_p` using the three fibre
   434	> relations `2 beta_p + t_p + a_p + eps_p = 4` (`beta_p = 2, t_p = 0` on
   435	> `Sing D_1 - D_0`; `beta_p = 1` on `D_1 ∩ D_0`; `beta_p = 0` on
   436	> `Sing D_0 - D_1`) together with `n_1 = sum_p beta_p`, `n_2 = sum_p k_p`. The
   437	> boundary points over `A_F - Sing A_F` are exactly the `s_l` dicritical points
   438	> by the promoted covering lemma, so `eps_p = 0` off `Sing A_F`. Every term
   439	> `s_0 k_p - t_p` is `>= 0` because `l_0' -> D~_0` has degree `s_0`. The
   440	> stated bounds follow from `r_1 >= 1`, `c_0 >= 1` by inspection of
