   527	> and the transposition horn with no H2 hypothesis. A weaker sufficient form
   528	> also suffices: *no surjection `pi_1(C^2-D) -> S_4` sends every meridian to a
   529	> transposition and the two local meridians at each double point to **disjoint**
   530	> transpositions* (Thm. 4.3(4)).
   531	>
   532	> Status of the literature on this lemma. Deligne–Fulton (Zariski's conjecture)
   533	> gives `pi_1(P^2 - C)` abelian for `C ⊂ P^2` irreducible **nodal**; Nori's
   534	> theorem gives abelianness under `C^2 > 2·#nodes`. Neither is quoted here
   535	> because (a) our `D` has one place at infinity, so `bar D ∪ L_∞` is never
   536	> nodal and the affine complement is not the projective one, and (b) our double
   537	> points are only known to be two *smooth* branches, which permits tangency.
