   406	exclusion is real.  The bundle nevertheless contains a false Route-1
   407	meta-theorem, a sign error in its claimed complete residual structure, an
   408	unlicensed H3-free use of `(M)`, and a false two-profile rank-five census.
   409	
   410	| Item | Recommendation and exact scope |
   411	|---|---|
   412	| Proposition 2.1 | **PROMOTE** the exponent/Jacobian dictionary for the alteration formulas, after replacing “same chart” by the qualified formulation in §3. |
   413	| Proposition 2.2 | **PROMOTE** for every affine-image map-dicritical of a Keller map. |
   414	| Proposition 2.3 | **DO NOT PROMOTE.** Replace it by: the determinant-order and gcd data alone do not exclude `l=k+1`. |
   415	| Lemmas 3.1–3.3 | **PROMOTE.** Purity is applied to finite `q`; Orevkov 5.2 is pointwise, with global zero correction a sufficient hypothesis. Type corrections on `pi(l)`. |
   416	| Lemma 3.4 | **PROMOTE** for irreducible `A_F`, `N>=3`, under either its smooth branch or “all corrections zero and `2a<=N`” branch, with the equality repair in §4. |
   417	| Theorem 3.5 | **PROMOTE verbatim** at that scope.  Its AMS/cyclic-monodromy endgame is sound. |
   418	| Corollary 3.6 | **PROMOTE the theorem**, but delete “strengthening of Chau 4.4”; call it an independent reproof. |
   419	| Corollary 3.7 | **PROMOTE** `sum mu_l<=N-2` under irreducible `A_F`; replace “locally irreducible singularity” by “critical point of an immersed parametrization.” |
   420	| Corollary 3.8 | **PROMOTE** for every noninvertible plane Keller map (the promoted degree floor supplies `N>=3`). |
   421	| Proposition 4.1 | **PROMOTE** at `N=4` (indeed its all-trivial argument is degree-independent once there is more than one sheet). |
   422	| Theorem 4.2 | **PROMOTE** under `N=4` and H2: no `mu=1`, unique `(2,1)` cost profile, `s_1=1,a=2,b=0,(delta,e)=(1,2)`, meridian a transposition, global group `S_4`.  Assert `(M)` only with H3, or insert and cite the checked affine-line-normalization lemma. |
   423	| Theorem 4.3(1)–(4) | **PROMOTE**, adding `Sing D_1 cap D_0=empty`. |
   424	| Theorem 4.3(5) | **REFUTED as printed.** Do not promote its `+epsilon` identity.  A promotable replacement deletes the extra `epsilon` term using Orevkov Lemma 2.1 and strengthens to `s_0=1` and both normalizations `A^1`, as in §7. |
   425	| Corollary 4.4 | **PROMOTE conditional on `r_1=1`;** it holds throughout the repaired residual configuration. |
   426	| Corollary 5.1 | **PROMOTE** under H2; at `N=5`, `m<=2`. |
   427	| Corollary 5.2 | **PROMOTE** only for the `N=4`, H2 horn. |
   428	| General-`N` OPEN | **RETAIN OPEN**, but at `N=5` replace “exactly two profiles” by the single `(2,1)+(1,0)` profile and record its covering degrees after the source repair. |
   429	
   430	On Deligne–Fulton/Nori: **the descriptions in the charged report do not yet
   431	decide the needed lemma.**  Deligne–Fulton concerns an irreducible projective
   432	curve with ordinary nodes, whereas
   433	`C^2-D=P^2-(bar D union L_infinity)` deletes a reducible divisor.  The affine
   434	double branches here may be tangent, and the one place at infinity can be a
   435	non-nodal singular/contact.  Abelianity of `pi_1(P^2-bar D)` would not by
   436	itself imply abelianity after additionally deleting `L_infinity`.  The
   437	report's former `C^*` alternative would moreover have two places at infinity,
   438	although the source repair removes it.
   439	
   440	Before either theorem can be invoked, an acquisition must check: (i) whether
   441	“double point” means ordinary transverse node; (ii) whether the theorem has
   442	an affine or reducible-divisor version; (iii) the exact projective closure and
   443	intersection multiplicity with `L_infinity`; (iv) for Nori, which strict or
   444	resolved divisor enters the self-intersection inequality and how infinitely
   445	near/tangent points are counted; and (v) whether the conclusion is full
   446	abelianity or merely centrality/commutativity of meridians sufficient to rule
   447	out the specified `S_4` representation.  If those checks fail, one must run
   448	van Kampen for `bar D union L_infinity` and test the prescribed transposition
   449	images.  This is not safely typed as a mere quotation lookup.
   450	
