codex
The key structural distinction is now clear: H2 gives one target curve, not two. The two dicriticals are degree-one copies of the same normalization. I’m recording the promoted premises with the three different notions of degree separated; this prevents the correction \(3-2\) from being misread as a curve multiplicity or Puiseux exponent.
apply patch
