+Indeed, let \(x_1=h_1^{-1}(z)\).  Since \(h_2\) is an isomorphism, the
+unique correction gives
+
+\[
+ 0=d\phi_2(x)=d\eta(z)\,dh_2(x),
+ \quad\text{hence}\quad d\eta(z)=0.                                  \tag{5.1}
+\]
+
