   252	
   253	The curve budget before imposing the second row is nevertheless precise:
   254	
   255	* \(D\) is a polynomial curve, \(\widetilde D\simeq\mathbf A^1\), with
   256	  one place at infinity;
   257	* its only affine singularity is \(p_*\), and \((D,p_*)\) is a single
   258	  primitive plane branch;
   259	* the correction point contributes zero to
   260	  \(\nu=\sum(r_p-1)\), but contributes \(a_{p_*}=1\) to the affine-fibre
   261	  term in (3.4); and
   262	* the critical normalization forces \(\delta_{p_*}\ge1\).  Since
   263	  \(r_{p_*}=1\), its Milnor number is
   264	  \(\mu_{\mathrm{Mil}}(p_*)=2\delta_{p_*}\ge2\).  This Milnor number is
   265	  unrelated to Orevkov's \(\mu_x=3\).
   266	
   267	The promoted Euler machinery contains \(r_p-1\), not \(\delta_p\), so it
   268	does not determine the last integer or a Puiseux characteristic.  The
   269	local models (2.3)--(2.6) exhibit, for example, budgets
   270	\(\delta=1\) for \((2,3)\), \(\delta=4\) for \((2,9)\), and
   271	\(\delta=3\) for \((3,4)\), all before the trivial dicritical is imposed.
   272	The second table row instead makes \(\eta\) immersive at \(z\); because
   273	the germ has only one branch, that forces it smooth and
   274	\(\delta_{p_*}=\mu_{\mathrm{Mil}}(p_*)=0\).  The two componentwise
   275	budgets are therefore incompatible.
   276	
   277	## 5. Verdict on the \(N=5\) profile
   278	
   279	**Verdict: the promoted profile self-destructs.**  This is not the
   280	\(N=4\) row-(d) strictness argument.  The Euler and fibre machinery first
   281	pins the arithmetically consistent shape (3.1), (3.6), (3.7); the two
   282	degree-one parametrizations then contradict one another.
   283	
   284	Indeed, let \(x_1=h_1^{-1}(z)\).  Since \(h_2\) is an isomorphism, the
   285	unique correction gives
   286	
   287	\[
   288	 0=d\phi_2(x)=d\eta(z)\,dh_2(x),
   289	 \quad\text{hence}\quad d\eta(z)=0.                                  \tag{5.1}
   290	\]
   291	
   292	Since \(h_1\) is also an isomorphism,
   293	
   294	\[
   295	 d\phi_1(x_1)=d\eta(z)\,dh_1(x_1)=0,                                 \tag{5.2}
   296	\]
   297	
   298	contrary to the everywhere-immersive \(\mu=1\) parametrization.  The
   299	argument does not identify a cv flag with a physical place: it compares
   300	the two distinct source points only after each has been mapped
   301	isomorphically to the same normalization place \(z\).  Nor does it use a
   302	lower bound as attainment.
   303	
   304	Consequently no Puiseux type is consistent with **all** of (1.1).  The
   305	ordinary cusp is not singled out and then excluded; rather, every
   306	possible critical normalization germ is excluded by the second
   307	degree-one copy of the normalization.  Thus the trivial-dicritical
   308	profile at \(N=5\) is impossible under H2.
   309	
   310	## 6. The exact PI1-S4-style residual question
   311	
   312	There is no genuine fundamental-group residual after §5.  For clarity,
   313	the question that would remain if one deliberately forgot the fatal
   314	\(\mu=1\) normalization copy is the following.
   315	
   316	> **Counterfactual `PI1-S5-CORR`.**  Let \(D\subset\mathbf C^2\) be an
   317	> irreducible polynomial curve normalized by \(\mathbf A^1\), with one
   318	> place at infinity and exactly one affine singular point \(p\), which is
   319	> unibranch.  Suppose the germ is the discriminant of a normal local
   320	> three-sheeted cover having generic simple ramification and one
   321	> local-degree-three point.  Can
   322	> \(\pi_1(\mathbf C^2-D)\) surject onto \(S_5\) so that every meridian of
   323	> \(D\) maps to a transposition and the local group at \(p\) has orbit
   324	> partition \((3,1,1)\), acting as \(S_3\) on the three-letter orbit and
   325	> fixing the other two letters?
   326	
   327	The \(S_5\) target is forced counterfactually: the branch locus is \(D\),
   328	the generic meridian has cycle type \((2,1,1,1)\), and connected global
   329	monodromy is a transitive group generated by transpositions, hence
   330	\(S_5\).  In the additional smooth-source/smooth-ramification subcase,
   331	\((D,p)\) is \(A_2\); the two standard local transpositions share one
   332	letter and generate the displayed \(S_3\), rather than being disjoint as
   333	in `PI1-S4`.
   334	
   335	This question is only the \(\pi_1\)-shadow of the numerical packet.  A
   336	YES would not realize the Keller configuration, because it omits the
   337	second degree-one parametrization.  The exact source-aware residual is
   338	
   339	> Can one normalization map \(\eta:\mathbf A^1\to D\) be critical at
   340	> \(z\) through one degree-one dicritical parametrization and immersive
   341	> at the same \(z\) through another?
   342	
   343	Equations (5.1)--(5.2) answer this **NO**.  Accordingly no
   344	`OPEN[PI1-S5-CORR]` should be entered and no PI1 acquisition is needed
   345	for this profile.
